# NOTICE

This project contains **no code** from deskflow, Synergy, Hyprland, aquamarine
or libei. It is an `LD_PRELOAD` shim that interposes four symbols exported by
`libei.so` at runtime, plus a test stub that defines the same four symbols with
trivial bodies.

The files under `docs/` quote short excerpts of MIT/GPL-licensed source and of
disassembly produced by `objdump` / `otool` for the purpose of documenting the
bug. Those excerpts remain under their original licenses:

| Component | License | Upstream |
|---|---|---|
| deskflow | GPL-2.0 | https://github.com/deskflow/deskflow |
| Synergy 3 | GPL-2.0 (core) / proprietary (GUI) | https://symless.com/synergy |
| Hyprland | BSD-3-Clause | https://github.com/hyprwm/Hyprland |
| aquamarine | BSD-3-Clause | https://github.com/hyprwm/aquamarine |
| libei | MIT | https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/libinput/libei |

The symbol names interposed (`ei_event_scroll_get_dx`, `ei_event_scroll_get_dy`,
`ei_event_scroll_get_discrete_dx`, `ei_event_scroll_get_discrete_dy`) are
libei's public API; naming them is required for interposition and is not a
derivative work.

`test/ei_stub.c` is an original file — it defines the four symbols with bodies
that return global variables so the unit test can run without a live session.

Trademarks belong to their respective owners. This is an independent,
unofficial workaround; it is not affiliated with or endorsed by Symless,
deskflow, or Hyprland.
